-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:142e56461e41cc1a296a562b387564c20aa1337b373c386b6e1b4219f1889f10","file":"preprints/Conditional-coordinate-sweeps-and-analytic-transfer-September-26-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":54,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"a4b0e9a2b3f7f5cce02f09638eee3bc2f400a6e675d0e8ea618ec3e3b98c9d41","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Conditional-coordinate-sweeps-and-analytic-transfer-September-26-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:142e56461e41cc1a296a562b387564c20aa1337b373c386b6e1b4219f1889f10","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Conditional-coordinate-sweeps-and-analytic-transfer-September-26-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L54"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:binary}\nThere are absolute constants \\(g>0\\) and \\(d_0\\) such that, for \\(d\\ge d_0\\)\nand every \\(\\lambda\\vdash 2^d\\),\n\\[\n \\|K_\\lambda\\|_{\\op}\\le D_\\lambda^{-g}.\n\\]\nThe sign representation is annihilated. There is an absolute positive integer \\(w\\)\nsuch that the law after \\(w\\) independent sweeps converges to uniform in\ntotal variation as \\(d\\to\\infty\\), uniformly over deterministic initial\ndecks."}
